# ========================
# DEBUGGING & DEVELOPMENT 
# ========================


# Sampling Sequences and Logic
# ----------------------------
# {<various>}
#
# The two forms say the same thing: a list of sampler names separated by ';',
# or the one-letter shorthand for the same list in the same order. Set one or
# the other. Letters: e penalties, d dry, s top_n_sigma, k top_k, y typ_p,
# p top_p, m min_p, x xtc, t temperature, i infill, a adaptive_p.
#
# Covers: --samplers / -s, --seed, --sampler-seq / --sampling-seq, --ignore-eos
#
# DROSTE_LLAMA_SAMPLERS="penalties;dry;top_n_sigma;top_k;typ_p;top_p;min_p;xtc;temperature"
# DROSTE_LLAMA_SAMPLING_SEQ="edskypmxt"
# DROSTE_LLAMA_SEED=-1                 # -1 = a new random seed per start
# DROSTE_LLAMA_IGNORE_EOS=off


# Logging & diagnostics
# ---------------------
# {auto*, on, off}, {<path>}, {0..4}, {on, off}
#
# The server logs to the box's service log, which is where Droste's own tools
# read it from; setting a log file writes a second copy. Verbosity is a
# threshold, so a higher number keeps more: 0 generic, 1 error, 2 warning,
# 3 info, 4 trace.
#
#   Covers: --log-colors, --log-file, -lv / --verbosity / --log-verbosity,
#           --log-prefix, --log-timestamps
#
# LLAMA_ARG_LOG_COLORS=auto
# LLAMA_ARG_LOG_FILE=                    # default: none, service log only
# LLAMA_ARG_LOG_VERBOSITY=3
# DROSTE_LLAMA_LOG_PREFIX=off
# DROSTE_LLAMA_LOG_TIMESTAMPS=off
#
#   Also reachable, through LLAMA_EXTRA_ARGS:
#     --check-tensors, --log-disable, --log-prompts-dir, --override-kv,
#     -v / --verbose / --log-verbose

# Fitting Output
